<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Franco-Hova War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1883">1883</a>–<a href="/years/1885">1885</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Franco-Hova War was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the Merina Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>, whose ruling class the French called Hova. French forces bombarded and occupied coastal towns, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toamasina">Tamatave</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahajanga">Majunga</a>, but could not advance inland. The treaty of December 1885 gave France control of Madagascar's foreign relations, the bay of Diego-Suarez and a resident-general in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antananarivo">Antananarivo</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/franco-hova-war.jpg" alt="Franco-Hova War" width="320" height="482" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Louis Bombled / Henri Galli · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LaGuerreAMadagascar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
